---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const description='Free India income tax calculator. Estimate tax under the new or old regime for FY 2024-25 (AY 2025-26) with slabs, rebate, and cess. Work stays in your browser.';
const jsonLd=[
{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:'https://deskutil.com/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'Finance',item:'https://deskutil.com/finance/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:3,name:'Income Tax Calculator',item:'https://deskutil.com/finance/income-tax-calculator/'}]},
{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'SoftwareApplication',name:'Income Tax Calculator',applicationCategory:'FinanceApplication',operatingSystem:'Any',url:'https://deskutil.com/finance/income-tax-calculator/',offers:{'@type':'Offer',price:'0',priceCurrency:'USD'},featureList:['New and old tax regime','FY 2024-25 / AY 2025-26 slabs','Standard deduction','Section 87A rebate','Health and education cess','Taxable income and total tax','Copy tax breakdown']},
{'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:[
{'@type':'Question',name:'Which financial year does this income tax calculator use?',acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:'Slabs and defaults follow India’s FY 2024-25 (assessment year 2025-26): new-regime Budget 2024 slabs with ₹75,000 standard deduction and section 87A rebate when taxable income is up to ₹7 lakh; old-regime slabs with ₹50,000 standard deduction and rebate when taxable income is up to ₹5 lakh. Health and education cess is 4% on tax after rebate.'}},
{'@type':'Question',name:'How is taxable income calculated?',acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:'Taxable income is gross annual income minus the standard deduction for the chosen regime, minus optional deductions you enter (for example section 80C under the old regime). Negative results are treated as zero. New-regime users often leave extra deductions at zero because many chapter VI-A deductions are not available there.'}},
{'@type':'Question',name:'How does the section 87A rebate work here?',acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:'Under the new regime, if taxable income is ₹7 lakh or less, rebate wipes out the tax before cess. Under the old regime, if taxable income is ₹5 lakh or less, rebate wipes out tax before cess. Cess is then applied to tax after rebate.'}},
{'@type':'Question',name:'Is this official income tax advice?',acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:'No. Results are planning estimates for resident individuals under 60. Surcharge for very high incomes, alternate deductions, and edge cases are simplified or omitted. This is not advice from the Income Tax Department and not financial advice.'}},
